Half Flush, so impossible.  \n\nGiven that, best is to aim for **All Types** \u2014 need a wind tile. Unshown F2=2, F3=3, F4=4 available. Maybe keep J1 and try to draw F.  \n\nBut drawing F could take time; easier is to go for **Two Dragon Pungs** (6 points) \u2014 need another J1 or J2/J3 pung. I have one J1 only. Unshown J1=2 left, possible but unlikely.  \n\nGiven game stage (many melds already), maybe just try to reduce points loss by discarding safest tile.  \n\nFrom history:  \n- Next player discarded T5 earlier, so T5 is relatively safe for next player.  \n- Across discarded B2 earlier, so B2 safe for across.  \n- Previous player\u2019s recent discards W4, W5 \u2014 so maybe W4/W5 safe for previous player.  \n\nBut B2, B3 are dangerous for previous? Previous player has B7 pung, maybe wants B8 B9.  \n\nActually safest seems J1 \u2014 dragons not obviously sought by anyone except maybe for pair.  \n\nBut let\u2019s check: across discarded J1, next player never discarded J1, previous player never discarded J1 \u2014 so next player might have J1 pair. Dangerous.  \n\nT5 discarded by next player, so safe for next player, but maybe across or previous need it? Across has T1 pung, so T5 not needed for T1-related. Previous has T9 pung, T8 discarded earlier.  \n\nI think T5 is safe.  \n\nBut if I discard T5, hand keeps J1, harder for All Simples.  \n\nGiven I need points, maybe better to discard J1 to open chance for All Simples and hope to draw W3/W6 for chow.  \n\n**Evaluation:**  \nPromising moves:  \n1. Play J1 \u2014 removes honor, aims for All Simples, but slightly risky if someone needs it for dragon pung.  \n2. Play T5 \u2014 safe discard, keeps honor for possible dragon pung chance.  \n3. Play B2 \u2014 safe based on across\u2019s discard, but B2 useful for B2 B3 B4 chow.  \n\nBest: Discard J1 to pursue All Simples + All Chows combination, which can reach 8+ points with extra patterns (Short Straight, Mixed Double Chow, etc.).  \n\n**Reason:**  \nDiscarding J1 allows the hand to aim for All Simples (2) + All Chows (2) + Short Straight (1) + Mixed Double Chow (1) + maybe Two Terminal Chows (1) \u2014 but no terminals here, so not. Actually need terminals for Two Terminal Chows, so no. But maybe Pure Double Chow (1) if I get another identical chow. Anyway, can reach 6\u20137 points plus Self Drawn (1) or Closed Wait (1) etc. to hit 8. Keeping J1 blocks All Simples and yields fewer patterns likely.  \n\n**Answer:** Play J1.  \n\nEvaluation: Discard J1 to aim for All Simples and All Chows patterns, increasing potential point combinations.  \nReason: J1 is an honor preventing All Simples; removing it opens more scoring patterns and the hand has potential to form multiple chows in Bamboo and Dots.  \nAnswer: Play J1"}
